---
import Announcement from "./Announcement.astro";
---

<section id="home-announcements" class="container mb-4">
  <div
    class="row row-cols-1 row-cols-md-2 row-cols-lg-3 g-4 mx-1 justify-content-center"
  >
    <Announcement
      title="Interested in Joining FAMNM?"
      image="offseason/2026/volunteers.jpg"
      alt="FAMNM volunteers on the field at the 2026 Wolverine Robotics Competition"
      links={[
        {
          text: "Calendar",
          link: "/members/calendar/",
        },
        {
          text: "Interest Form",
          link: "https://forms.gle/tuHsm3udnLim2a296",
        },
      ]}
    >
      Any U-M Ann Arbor student can join, with any level of <i>FIRST</i>
      experience. General Body Meetings are <b>Wednesdays, 8&ndash;9 PM in
      DOW 1018</b>, alternating with socials. Check the calendar for this
      week's meeting and fill out the interest form to get added to our Slack.
    </Announcement>
    <Announcement
      title="FTC Workshops"
      image="teams/ftc-workshop-2025.jpg"
      alt="FAMNM members reviewing an engineering notebook with an FTC team"
      links={[
        {
          text: "Learn more!",
          link: "/teams/workshops/",
        },
      ]}
    >
      Our FTC Engineering Notebook &amp; Presentation Seminars give teams
      practice judge interviews and feedback on their engineering portfolios.
      Fall 2026 sessions are <b>Tuesday, October 27, 7&ndash;8:30 PM</b> and
      <b>Tuesday, November 17, 6:30&ndash;8 PM</b>.
    </Announcement>
    <Announcement
      title="FRC Kickoff & Robot in 3 Days"
      image="kickoff/2026/stamps-crowd.jpg"
      alt="FRC teams filling Stamps Auditorium at FAMNM's 2026 FRC Kickoff"
      links={[
        {
          text: "FRC Kickoff",
          link: "/events/kickoff/",
        },
        {
          text: "Ri3D",
          link: "/events/ri3d/",
        },
      ]}
    >
      FAMNM will host FRC Kickoff for the 2027 season, BIOCORE, on
      <b>Saturday, January 9, 2027</b>. In the 72 hours that follow, our Ri3D
      team designs, builds, and drives a competition-ready robot and shares
      the whole process with teams around the world.
    </Announcement>
  </div>
</section>
